2026-11-17 22:04:06 - Agent_20261117215829 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed CodeQL findings for dangerous URL scheme handling in JSON schema validators. Identified and confirmed 4 true positive vulnerabilities across the jsonschema/validators.py file:

1. Line 112: Unsafe urlopen() call in _warn_for_remote_retrieve() - accepts file:// and other dangerous URL schemes
2. Line 113: Unsafe urlopen() call in _warn_for_remote_retrieve() - accepts file:// and other dangerous URL schemes  
3. Line 1225: Unsafe requests.get() call in resolve_remote() - accepts file:// and other dangerous URL schemes
4. Line 1228: Unsafe urlopen() call in resolve_remote() - accepts file:// and other dangerous URL schemes

All vulnerabilities stem from the same root cause: user-controlled URIs from JSON schema $ref fields are passed directly to HTTP/file fetching functions without URL scheme validation, allowing attackers to access local files via file:// URLs or potentially other dangerous schemes.

Data flow analysis confirmed that the `uri` parameter flows directly from the function arguments to the vulnerable sink functions without sanitization.
